// Phase 5C Task 2, design §3.4.1: whether pixi's `miterLimit: 10` and
// Lottie's `ml: 10` agree on the same ratio (SVG's `1/sin(theta/2)`, theta
// the corner's interior angle). Two lines, thickness 20, with a corner whose
// interior angle sits on opposite sides of the two candidate readings'
// cutoff at ratio 10: `miter14` at 14 degrees (ratio ~8.206, MITERED under
// the SVG reading) and `miter9` at 9 degrees (ratio ~12.745, BEVELLED).
//
// Each line is three points forming a symmetric peak (a "tent"): two legs
// each 100 units long, meeting at a vertex. `origin: (0.5, 0)` puts each
// line's pivot exactly at that vertex (the bbox's horizontal centre and its
// minimum y), so `position` names the vertex's own world coordinate
// directly -- verified by `localPivot`'s formula: bbox.min + origin*size
// collapses to (0,0) for a symmetric peak with origin.y=0.
//
// Confirmed directly by calling pixi.js's own `buildLine` (the exact
// function `Graphics.stroke()` runs) outside a browser, on these two point
// sets: `miter14` produces a joint vertex at distance 82.055 from the
// vertex along the bisector (matching 10/sin(7deg) exactly, a real miter
// spike); `miter9` produces its farthest joint vertices at distance 10.000
// (the plain per-segment offset, i.e. a flat BEVEL edge, not a spike
// reaching 127.45). So the sample point 30 units above each vertex, along
// the upward bisector -- comfortably beyond where either bevel edge sits
// (at or below the vertex itself) and comfortably short of a 14-degree
// miter's reach (82) -- discriminates cleanly: filled for a genuine miter,
// background for a genuine bevel, regardless of which of the two candidate
// `ml` readings a renderer actually implements.
scene {
  size: (500, 300)
  duration: 0.0333333333
  background: #000000

  line miter14 {
    position: (150, 150)
    origin: (0.5, 0)
    points: [(12.1869, 99.2546), (0, 0), (-12.1869, 99.2546)]
    thickness: 20
    color: #ffffff
  }

  line miter9 {
    position: (350, 150)
    origin: (0.5, 0)
    points: [(7.8459, 99.6917), (0, 0), (-7.8459, 99.6917)]
    thickness: 20
    color: #ffffff
  }
}
